{"step_index":73,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T21:01:53Z","input_tokens":2133,"cache_read_tokens":73092,"output_tokens":1429,"thinking":"The error indicates a CORS policy violation, specifically a blocked cross-origin request. The browser is preventing access to the `firebase-config.js` file due to the `file://` origin, which is not permitted for cross-origin requests. It seems that the browser's security features are correctly blocking the script.\n\n\nThe CORS error stems from the browser's security restrictions on cross-origin requests when accessing files via the `file://` protocol. Specifically, the ES module import from a local file (`firebase-config.js`) is blocked due to the `null` origin associated with `file://`. An important question: does importing from `https://www.gstatic.com/...` within a `<script type=\"module\">` also fail under `file:///`? It's necessary to verify if this specific setup circumvents the restriction.\n\n\nThe CORS error confirms a restriction on local file access via `file://` due to cross-origin request policies. The issue arises from relative module imports within a `<script type=\"module\">` tag, such as importing `./firebase-config.js`. An experiment is required: confirm if importing from a `https://` source, within the same setup, is also blocked under `file:///`.\n\nI'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html>\\n<head><title>Test File Origin</title></head>\\n<body>\\n<h1 id=\\\"out\\\">Testing...</h1>\\n<script type=\\\"module\\\">\\n  try {\\n    import(\\\"https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.14.0/firebase-app.js\\\")\\n      .then(mod => {\\n        document.getElementById(\\\"out\\\").textContent = \\\"Success loading gstatic from file://\\\";\\n      })\\n      .catch(err => {\\n        document.getElementById(\\\"out\\\").textContent = \\\"Error loading gstatic: \\\" + err.message;\\n      });\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    document.getElementById(\\\"out\\\").textContent = \\\"Catch error: \\\" + e.message;\\n  }\\n</script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n\"","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\CxAdmin\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\\\scratch\\\\test_file_origin.html\""}}]}
