{"step_index":84,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T21:02:26Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-09T05:02:26+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-09T05:02:29+08:00\nThe search for \"javascript \"from origin 'null' has been blocked by CORS policy\" type=\"module\" file://\" returned the following summary:\nThis error occurs because you are trying to open an HTML file directly in your browser using the local file system (`file://` protocol) while using JavaScript modules (`type=\"module\"`)[1][2]. \n\nModern browsers enforce a strict security policy (CORS) that blocks JavaScript modules from loading local files via `file://` because local files have an origin of `\"null\"`[2][3]. JavaScript modules **must** be loaded via an HTTP server (`http://` or `https://`)[1].\n\nTo fix this, you need to run your project through a local development server instead of double-clicking the HTML file[1]. Here are the easiest ways to do it:\n\n### 1. If you use Visual Studio Code (Recommended)\n1. Install the **Live Server** extension by Ritwick Dey from the VS Code Marketplace[1].\n2. Open your project folder in VS Code.\n3. Open your `index.html` file, right-click anywhere in the editor, and select **\"Open with Live Server\"**[1].\n4. It will automatically open your page in the browser via `http://127.0.0.1:...` and the error will disappear.\n\n### 2. Using Node.js (`npx serve`)\nIf you have Node.js installed on your computer, you don't even need to install a package permanently. Open your project folder in your terminal and run[1]:\n```bash\nnpx serve\n```\nThen, open the local URL (usually `http://localhost:3000`) provided in the terminal.\n\n### 3. Using Python\nIf you have Python installed, open your project folder in your terminal and run:\n* **Python 3:**\n  ```bash\n  python -m http.server\n  ```\n* **Python 2:**\n  ```bash\n  python -m SimpleHTTPServer\n  ```\nThen, open your browser and go to `http://localhost:8000`.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Checklist:\n* **Don't do this:** Double-clicking `index.html` so the address bar starts with `file:///`[1].\n* **Do this:** Run a local server so the address bar starts with `http://localhost:...` or `http://127.0.0.1:...`[1].\n\nSources:\n[1] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHXUOQceL0HWUQny8VxTZ51XySDJgEe-LJgYdi6YT_EttxwY3ue8YHQ7wdDSnVafeb0DYqISzJ5qc1UBTv_Ay_Wuk3Jt50tR4JJO66d04XYVeF_91VRxUddEtoWTOL9IEFXOqrf9dTWbl0gShwKR8ca4ilJo1bYVv9U0MIMpOeo24-c5NEbCB5Wz88ys9v7frGSeZHWGdik4pJt-3UKuTB1MR6RnxH7Ng==)\n[2] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFw3MKnoDKKmf7gkryTOTlwfKLgIdqtpzsJpSIpQcIs2enOgPIW05FEIiBqzfAhmU9RuL6BRq5i6gEtHe0ToxaQ5lgBIShydBMsbNqAqZ6tFhPYE5IuXkpl83ht01Govi6KY4mwJcbDdccp6WrdAGqfbuOG5aSHy1rFD9g0xHGOqKrkzzkUC5CrT4d_oXIT9O_NUh7Om6q8b7pz_9GIJJaVqXKZRF27309P38ioUUOs)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGobT1QzPfIYgg84MKCwE3nhRU2IiQpAECYK2s8YjHb4hw_mvLehN862lOoT1zMWT2wrFhaAw32gMNKc7Qy8UT3XUh6RsMhDzQho7G3Qs4uTcNj5g5ddv4lhjdY4gcoS2s=)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
{"step_index":85,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T21:02:29Z","input_tokens":3273,"cache_read_tokens":75741,"output_tokens":612,"thinking":"The double-click from Windows Explorer opens an HTML file with a `file:///` origin. Relative imports from the HTML file fail due to CORS restrictions, because of the `null` origin. Success hinges on finding a method to bypass this CORS issue, even when the file is opened locally.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html>\\n<head><title>Test Fetch</title></head>\\n<body>\\n<div id=\\\"status\\\">Testing...</div>\\n<script>\\n  const apiKey = \\\"AIzaSyBkqJ9WvtXfGJt19XK7SLK9v5cJwp4EVII\\\";\\n  const projectId = \\\"sir-jasper-quiz\\\";\\n  const url = `https://firestore.googleapis.com/v1/projects/${projectId}/databases/(default)/documents/quizzes/active?key=${apiKey}`;\\n\\n  fetch(url)\\n    .then(r => r.json())\\n    .then(data => {\\n      document.getElementById(\\\"status\\\").textContent = \\\"FETCH SUCCESS: \\\" + data.fields.title.stringValue;\\n    })\\n    .catch(err => {\\n      document.getElementById(\\\"status\\\").textContent = \\\"FETCH ERROR: \\\" + err.message;\\n    });\\n</script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n\"","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\CxAdmin\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\\\scratch\\\\test_fetch.html\""}}]}
