{"step_index":106,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T21:03:44Z","input_tokens":2129,"cache_read_tokens":86083,"output_tokens":2287,"thinking":"The test case executed successfully under the `file:///` protocol. The key observation is the use of standard `<script>` tags to load Firebase compat libraries, which avoids any CORS issues in this local context. The JavaScript code's execution appears unaffected by the file:// protocol.\n\n\nThe Firebase SDK functions seamlessly over HTTPS without origin restrictions, confirming expected behavior. This confirms identical functionality whether accessed locally via file protocol or hosted online. The user experience is simplified, eliminating the need for a local web server, build steps, or terminal commands for either local access or Vercel deployment. Now to analyze the rules to determine the patch entry.\n\n\nInitial investigation reveals the root cause of the CORS error as the browser's restriction on relative ES module imports from a 'null' origin when accessing files via the `file:///` protocol. The solution involves migrating from relative imports to standalone compat scripts, as the current structure is blocked. The current strategy will be to update the implementation plan, following the mandatory execution workflow.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":true,\"Summary\":\"Updated implementation plan to resolve file:/// origin null CORS blocking by transitioning to Firebase compat scripts, enabling dual-mode execution for local double-clicking and Vercel cloud deployment.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","Content":"\"# Implementation Plan: Resolve file:/// Protocol CORS Blocking for Local & Cloud Execution\\n\\n## 1. Problem Diagnosis & Root Cause\\nWhen opening `index.html` or `teacher.html` directly from the local file system (double-clicking the `.html` file in Windows Explorer, loading via `file:///C:/...`):\\n- Browsers assign the document an opaque origin of `\\\"null\\\"`.\\n- Under the browser Same-Origin Policy (SOP), `<script type=\\\"module\\\">` is blocked from importing other local files (`import { ... } from \\\"./firebase-config.js\\\"`), triggering:\\n  `Access to script at 'file:///...' from origin 'null' has been blocked by CORS policy: Cross origin requests are only supported for protocol schemes: chrome-extension, chrome-untrusted, data, edge, http, https, isolated-app.`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Solution & Architectural Optimization\\nReplace the relative ES module imports with the official Google Firebase compat CDN scripts:\\n- `https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.14.0/firebase-app-compat.js`\\n- `https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.14.0/firebase-firestore-compat.js`\\n\\n### Key Advantages:\\n1. **Dual-Mode Compatibility**:\\n   - Works immediately when double-clicked directly from Windows Explorer (`file:///` protocol) without needing any local server, terminal, or build process.\\n   - Works identically when deployed to Vercel, Netlify, or any HTTP/HTTPS web host.\\n2. **Zero CORS Blocking**: Standard `<script src=\\\"...\\\">` tags to `gstatic.com` are not restricted by origin `\\\"null\\\"`, and Firestore's network transport communicates freely over HTTPS from any origin.\\n3. **DRY & Maintainable**: Eliminates cross-file relative module resolution hurdles while keeping full Firebase Firestore functionality intact.\\n4. **Zero In-Code Comments (Rule 9)**: Preserves strict constraint of zero comments or docstrings across all files.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Proposed File Changes\\n\\n### 3.1 [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html)\\n- Replace `<script type=\\\"module\\\">` importing `./firebase-config.js` with direct script inclusi\n<truncated 2030 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\CxAdmin\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\\\implementation_plan.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls