{"step_index":108,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T21:04:03Z","input_tokens":2383,"cache_read_tokens":88217,"output_tokens":408,"content":"I have investigated the cause of the `CORS policy: origin 'null'` error and prepared a plan to fix it:\n\n### Cause:\nWhen double-clicking an HTML file directly from Windows Explorer (`file:///...`), the browser sets its origin to `'null'`. Under modern browser security rules, `<script type=\"module\">` is blocked from loading another relative local file (`./firebase-config.js`).\n\n### Solution:\nSwitch to the official Google Firebase CDN compat scripts:\n- `https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.14.0/firebase-app-compat.js`\n- `https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.14.0/firebase-firestore-compat.js`\n\nThis makes both [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html) and [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html) **dual-mode**:\n1. They work immediately when double-clicked directly from Windows Explorer (`file:///`) with **zero CORS errors**.\n2. They continue to work identically when deployed to **Vercel** or any web server.\n\nPlease review the updated [implementation_plan.md](file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/.gemini/antigravity/brain/8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a/implementation_plan.md).\n\nMay I have your approval to implement this fix? (You can reply directly in text or click the Proceed button on the implementation plan artifact)."}
